message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "vxmodels: SysML v2 models and the model-to-manifest renderer of the vxedge testbed"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Djaafri"
    given-names: "Fouzi"
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher"
repository-code: "https://github.com/vxedge/vxmodels"
url: "https://vxedge.dev"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-10-29"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - sysml
  - mbse
  - software-defined-vehicle
  - automotive
  - testbed
  - reproducible-research
  - rust
abstract: >-
  vxmodels holds the SysML v2 models that govern vxedge (requirements H1-H4 with verification
  links, vehicle E/E structure, experiments as analysis cases) and vxmodel, a Rust renderer that
  turns them into vxedge workspace manifests, each gated by vxedge manifest validation. The model is
  the design authority; manifests remain the only execution contract. It is not a general-purpose
  SysML v2 toolchain. The Rust code is Apache-2.0; the SysML models and documentation are CC BY 4.0
  (LICENSE-DOCS).
references:
  - type: software
    title: "vxedge: specification and results of an all-software SDV network-slicing testbed"
